@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: WWW Press Release
	Frontend testing for creating a www press release

Setup:
    * I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I sign out and sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	* I tear down the following web content entries
	| Our Latest and Greatest Press Release |
	| Scheduled press release               |
	| American Press Release                |
	
Scenario: Add Press Release
	Admins should be able to add a press release on www.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the Sign In Create Account footer link
	And I sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	And I navigate to the Product Menu and go to the "Web Content" portlet under the "Content & Data" category under the "Site Administration" panel
	And I go to the web content folder "COMPANY"
	And I go to the web content folder "PRESS RELEASES"
	And I go to a new form for a "Press Release" web content
	And I expand the "Categorization" header in the side panel
	And I populate the following web content fields and values
	| Title                |                 | Our Latest and Greatest Press Release                               |
	| Heading              | Input           | The Latest News From Liferay                                        |
	| Subheading           | Input           | We have lots to tell you                                            |
	| Content              | Textarea        | Plenty has happened at Liferay and we cannot wait to share with you |
	| Category List Filter | Category Select | Press Releases                                                      |
	| Language             | Category Select | English                                                             |
	| Location             | Category Select | United States                                                       |
	| News Type            | Category Select | Company                                                             |
	| type                 | Category Select | press-release                                                       |
	| Year                 | Category Select | 2020                                                                |
	And I click the publish button
	And I sign out of www
#	And I go to the www page with the url "press-releases"
#	Then the following text should be visible on the page
#	| Our Latest and Greatest Press Release |
	When I go to the www page with the url "press-release?title=our-latest-and-greatest-press-release"
	Then the following text should be visible on the page
	| The Latest News From Liferay                                        |
	| We have lots to tell you                                            |
	| Plenty has happened at Liferay and we cannot wait to share with you |

Scenario: Schedule Press Release
	Admins should be able to schedule a press release on www.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the Sign In Create Account footer link
	And I sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	And I navigate to the Product Menu and go to the "Web Content" portlet under the "Content & Data" category under the "Site Administration" panel
	And I go to the web content folder "COMPANY"
	And I go to the web content folder "PRESS RELEASES"
	And I go to a new form for a "Press Release" web content
	And I expand the "Categorization" header in the side panel
	And I expand the "Schedule" header in the side panel
	And I populate the following web content fields and values
	| Title                |                 | Scheduled press release                                          |
	| Heading              | Input           | Scheduled News From Liferay                                      |
	| Subheading           | Input           | We have lots to tell you but we had to wait a bit                |
	| Content              | Textarea        | Plenty has happened at Liferay but we didn't tell you right away |
	| Category List Filter | Category Select | Press Releases                                                   |
	| Language             | Category Select | English                                                          |
	| Location             | Category Select | United States                                                    |
	| News Type            | Category Select | Company                                                          |
	| type                 | Category Select | press-release                                                    |
	| Year                 | Category Select | 2020                                                             |
	And I change the display date to "6" minutes into the future
	And I click the publish button
	And I sign out of www
#	And I go to the www page with the url "press-releases"
#	Then the following text should not be visible on the page
#	| Scheduled press release |
	When I go to the www page with the url "press-release?title=scheduled-press-release"
	Then the following text should not be visible on the page
	| Scheduled News From Liferay                                      |
	| We have lots to tell you but we had to wait a bit                |
	| Plenty has happened at Liferay but we didn't tell you right away |
	When I wait for "30" minutes
#	And I go to the www page with the url "press-releases"
#	Then the following text should be visible on the page
#	| Scheduled press release |
	When I go to the www page with the url "press-release?title=scheduled-press-release"
	Then the following text should be visible on the page
	| Scheduled News From Liferay                                      |
	| We have lots to tell you but we had to wait a bit                |
	| Plenty has happened at Liferay but we didn't tell you right away |

Scenario: Localize Press Release
	Admins should be able to localize a press release on www.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the Sign In Create Account footer link
	And I sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	And I navigate to the Product Menu and go to the "Web Content" portlet under the "Content & Data" category under the "Site Administration" panel
	And I go to the web content folder "COMPANY"
	And I go to the web content folder "PRESS RELEASES"
	And I go to a new form for a "Press Release" web content
	And I expand the "Categorization" header in the side panel
	And I populate the following web content fields and values
	| Title                |                 | American Press Release                                       |
	| Heading              | Input           | News from the United States                                  |
	| Subheading           | Input           | News concerning our American Market                          |
	| Content              | Textarea        | We have much to tell you about our operations in Los Angeles |
	| Category List Filter | Category Select | Press Releases                                               |
	| Language             | Category Select | English                                                      |
	| Location             | Category Select | United States                                                |
	| News Type            | Category Select | Company                                                      |
	| type                 | Category Select | press-release                                                |
	| Year                 | Category Select | 2020                                                         |
	And I change the current localization to "en-AU"
	And I clear the following existing web content fields
	| Heading    | Input    |
	| Subheading | Input    |
	| Content    | Textarea |
	And I populate the following web content fields and values
	| Heading    | Input    | News from the across the pond                                     |
	| Subheading | Input    | News concerning our friends in the states                         |
	| Content    | Textarea | We have much to tell you about what the Americans have been doing |
	And I click the publish button
	And I sign out of www
#	And I go to the www page with the url "press-releases"
#	Then the following text should be visible on the page
#	| American Press Release |
	When I go to the www page with the url "press-release?title=american-press-release"
	Then the following text should be visible on the page
	| News from the United States                                  |
	| News concerning our American Market                          |
	| We have much to tell you about our operations in Los Angeles |
	And the following text should not be visible on the page
	| News from the across the pond                                     |
	| News concerning our friends in the states                         |
	| We have much to tell you about what the Americans have been doing |
	When I change the language of the site to "Australian English"
	Then the following text should be visible on the page
	| News from the across the pond                                     |
	| News concerning our friends in the states                         |
	| We have much to tell you about what the Americans have been doing |
	And the following text should not be visible on the page
	| News from the United States                                  |
	| News concerning our American Market                          |
	| We have much to tell you about our operations in Los Angeles |	